{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380939-musing-on-a-merit-ennui","id":1380939,"title":"Musing on a merit: Ennui","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-13T07:43:08-07:00","id":1380939,"title":"Musing on a merit: Ennui","content":"While listening to Hadestown, and thinking about Gods and other spirits innured and jaded to beauty through the dint of ages...<br /> <br /> <b>Ennui</b><br /> <i>Story Merit, rated * to ***</i><br /> <br /> Over the course of decades and centuries, overexposure to wonders can begin to seem commonplace. Characters with the Ennui merit have witnessed so many works of staggering beauty that they are simply harder to impress through such means.<br /> <br /> Characters add their Ennui to their Resolve for the purposes of resisting Performance-based social influence actions, as well as for calculating the effect of another's Appearance. Should a Performance-based social influence action succeed against them, they must spend an additional amount of Willpower equal to their Ennui in order to resist; being so jaded, they are more touched when something breaks through their cynical exterior.<br /> <br /> Ennui 1 examples: Jaded Cynis sybarite, ghosts over a century old<br /> Ennui 2 examples: First Age survivors, most spirits<br /> Ennui 3 examples: World-founding titans, gods who regularly witness the Games of Divinity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 04-13-2020, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T07:51:39-07:00","id":1380943,"title":"","content":"Seems to make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T08:03:48-07:00","id":1380950,"title":"","content":"I'd never buy it. A merit that makes me spend extra Willpower? Hard pass.<br /> <br /> I'd rather take an appropriate Principle to represent my ennui.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T08:14:19-07:00","id":1380953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380939-musing-on-a-merit-ennui?p=1380950#post1380950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd never buy it. A merit that makes me spend extra Willpower? Hard pass.<br /> <br /> I'd rather take an appropriate Principle to represent my ennui.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, a Principle of &quot;I'm so jaded&quot; is more of a decision someone has made about themselves; it's like a teenager that has decided they be will a world-weary cynic.<br /> <br /> Which is a thing, but it's a different thing than someone that is world-weary because of their life experiences.<br /> <br /> (Also, it's more of an NPC merit)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T08:23:45-07:00","id":1380958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380939-musing-on-a-merit-ennui?p=1380953#post1380953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me, a Principle of &quot;I'm so jaded&quot; is more of a decision someone has made about themselves</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't read Initimacies this way.<br /> <br /> If the Realm burns your village to the ground and leaves you with an Intimacy of &quot;Hatred of the Realm&quot;, then that's not a decision you've made for yourself -- it's the result of your life experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T08:30:05-07:00","id":1380965,"title":"","content":"I'm also not a huge fan of the &quot;spend extra willpower&quot; thing. I'd suggest that Ennui 1 has no drawback, while 2 and 3 have the effect of intensifying any applicable Intimacy or emotion, once the Perform roll succeeds. So if someone was trying to inspire an emotion of lust, it now has a strength equivalent to a Defining Intimacy (as opposed to Major, the default), while if they were making an instill action, the Intimacy is modified one additional step higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T09:40:40-07:00","id":1380997,"title":"","content":"I'm with JohnDoe244 on this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T13:20:02-07:00","id":1381074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380939-musing-on-a-merit-ennui?p=1380958#post1380958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't read Initimacies this way.<br /> <br /> If the Realm burns your village to the ground and leaves you with an Intimacy of &quot;Hatred of the Realm&quot;, then that's not a decision you've made for yourself -- it's the result of your life experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you can get over your hatred of the Realm.<br /> <br /> The concept being expressed through this Merit of Ennui doesn't seem like something you can just get over. In a sense, it's less a Merit and more a Derangement. You've simply been exposed to too much greatness and terribleness in life to react as strongly to things, anymore. Your sense of scale has been changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T14:50:08-07:00","id":1381104,"title":"","content":"I feel like for an NPC, the effect of &quot;they are more touched when something breaks through their cynical exterior&quot; should be something that the Storyteller handles on a case-by-case basis - it seems like something that should be highlighted at the appropriate narrative moment, not handled through mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T15:22:36-07:00","id":1381119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380939-musing-on-a-merit-ennui?p=1381074#post1381074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you can get over your hatred of the Realm.<br /> <br /> The concept being expressed through this Merit of Ennui doesn't seem like something you can just get over. In a sense, it's less a Merit and more a Derangement. You've simply been exposed to too much greatness and terribleness in life to react as strongly to things, anymore. Your sense of scale has been changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the OP it talks about being touched by an especially moving experience. Now that might be a one-and-done, but equally couldn't that rekindle a sense of wonder? But I wouldn't be opposed to having ennui as a Flaw.<br /> <br /> IDK. True Love was a Merit in oWoD. I wouldn't like to see it ported to 3E Exalted, even though the Merit, did and represented something different to an Exalted Intimacy. Same for True Faith. Heck, &quot;Nightclub&quot; was a Merit distinct from Resources back in the day. If we're handing out custom Merits for &quot;ennui&quot; then where does it end?<br /> <br /> Is your NPC already at Resolve 5? Can't you just give them +1 Resolve? Or an Integrity Specailty? Is the Willpower thing even a drawback for an NPC whom you're probably not tracking Willpower recovery on anyway?<br /> <br /> If you want to use this in your games then use it. I won't be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-14-2020, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T14:14:24-07:00","id":1381764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380939-musing-on-a-merit-ennui?p=1381119#post1381119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is your NPC already at Resolve 5? Can't you just give them +1 Resolve?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is bad advice, imo. I don't like the idea of giving NPCs arbitrarily inflated stats for no reason other than to make things more difficult. If it can't be justified by magic or identifiable circumstances, then it shouldn't be done, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T15:27:52-07:00","id":1381777,"title":"","content":"I'm not exactly a big fan of &quot;lol fuck ur app roflmao&quot;, it was bad in 2e and it's still uncool in 3e. Why does your jadedness have more narrative significance than my legendary beauty, especially given the latter costs way more to obtain (40xp, 30 favored, plus possibly charms with commensurate commitment costs, vs like 9xp)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T06:16:59-07:00","id":1381904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380939-musing-on-a-merit-ennui?p=1381777#post1381777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not exactly a big fan of &quot;lol fuck ur app roflmao&quot;, it was bad in 2e and it's still uncool in 3e. Why does your jadedness have more narrative significance than my legendary beauty, especially given the latter costs way more to obtain (40xp, 30 favored, plus possibly charms with commensurate commitment costs, vs like 9xp)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because exaggerated attributes (especially beauty / appearance) are common among Gods, and the difficulty scale in Exalted means that legendary performances are commonplace in Heaven.<br /> <br /> Basically, I was listening to Hadestown, which got me thinking about Orpheus, which led me to imaging a song so beautiful it stayed Saturn's hand, and how much *better* that song would need to be to shine against the backdrop of Heaven's beauty.<br /> <br /> (Also, as a story merit, it's not one you could just buy after character creation, and one that most PCs would have some difficulty justifying)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T11:08:44-07:00","id":1381952,"title":"","content":"A thought. Maybe Ennui should be all or nothing?<br /> You add it to Resolve to determine if you're affected by the Appearance rating of the person trying to influence you and if you are then you're impressed and they use your unmodified Resolve to determine the dice bonus. So, for example. The Cynis is hardened against mundane beauty but influenced as normal by something supernatural rather than &quot;I went to Yu-Shan, it was okay I guess&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-16-2020, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T15:21:50-07:00","id":1381996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380939-musing-on-a-merit-ennui?p=1381764#post1381764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is bad advice, imo. I don't like the idea of giving NPCs arbitrarily inflated stats for no reason other than to make things more difficult. If it can't be justified by magic or identifiable circumstances, then it shouldn't be done, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>QCs don't have Wits or Integrity. If you can't justify why one of those stats should be higher than it is, but can justify ennui, then I suggest a Specialy or Intimacy of ennui.<br /> <br /> NPCs have the stats you invent them to have. What's the story goal here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T10:04:03-07:00","id":1382191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1380939-musing-on-a-merit-ennui?p=1381996#post1381996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">QCs don't have Wits or Integrity. If you can't justify why one of those stats should be higher than it is, but can justify ennui, then I suggest a Specialy or Intimacy of ennui.<br /> <br /> NPCs have the stats you invent them to have. What's the story goal here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they have the stats you want them to have. I'm saying they shouldn't be having Wits 8 &amp; Integrity 14 just because the PC in question has 20 dice with their Charms. I've seen things like that happen, inflating static values to double digits just to try and put a damper on the PCs plans. I am strongly advocating against doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/memb